  {
   "at": "2026-11-18T16:32:15+00:00",
   "cleared": "deepseek-neither: provenance: deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813 on deepinfra/fp8 was asked for and null answered",
   "why": "Not a provenance failure: OpenRouter answered HTTP 200 with a whitespace-only body (keep-alive padding, no JSON) at deepseek-neither c19, Fern's 5th call; the harness judged provenance on any 200. Fixed (an empty or unparseable 200 is a retryable error; provenance is judged only on a parsed answer); the stop cleared and the world resumed from its saved turn. The dropped call stays in the record as Fern's «(no reply)»."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-18T23:45:00+00:00",
   "what": "llmapi «HTTP 400 invalid_request_error: Operation not allowed»",
   "why": "From about 22:30 UTC llmapi answered a share of Haiku 5.5 calls this way (Bedrock route; the first-party route too, 1 of 12), trivial prompts included, and a failing prompt usually succeeds when sent again — a gateway error that never reached the model, not a refusal. Probes: 2 of 12, 2 of 12, then 7 of 16 trivial «Reply with the single word: ok» calls failed; 6 of the 7 succeeded on all three retries. The rate in mixed-both reached about 35% around 23:40. Before the fix the harness did not retry a 4xx: deepseek-neither's last cycles lost 56 welfare checks (not checked, never a flag) and mixed-both lost 12 Haiku citizen turns («(no reply)») and 82 checks; from 23:24 UTC the error is retried like an overload (pilot.mjs RETRYABLE). The 97 probe calls were not metered; booked here as an upper estimate."
  },
  {
   "at": "2026-11-18T23:45:00+00:00",
   "what": "mixed-both restarts",
   "why": "Restarted at 23:24 UTC at a turn boundary (after c15 heath) to load the retry; killed by a container restart at about 23:38 mid-turn (c16 gale) and resumed from its save at 23:40 — the partial turn's calls were made again."
  }
